{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ humility (+ \"leads to happiness\" \"lead to happiness\" \"makes us happy\" \"happier\"))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_28_672357894#5_1448460934","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q3086","rank":1,"snippet":"\": 4824.000000 , \"headings\": \"The Seventh Step of Alcoholics Anonymous: Developing Humility The Seventh Step of Alcoholics Anonymous: Developing Humility Defining Humility The Importance of Developing Humility 5 Ways to Practice Humility in Your Recovery Practice Gratitude Be Yourself Don’t Be Afraid to Learn Practice Kindness Learn to Be Free \" , \"segment\": \"These previous steps allowed you to start cultivating and practicing humility and the act of letting go those shortcomings that marked your past life will help you become <cover>happier, more fulfilled and more spiritually connected. 5 Ways to Practice Humility </cover>in Your Recovery If you are about to work or are currently working the Seventh Step of AA, the following five ways can help humility flourish in your recovery and your life: Practice Gratitude It is important to look at what positive attributes you have and how you can share them with others. Practicing gratitude in your recovery on a daily basis will allow you to truly be grounded within yourself without bragging or have an inflated sense of worth. Be Yourself Don’t fall into the trap with comparing yourself to other people. "}}
