{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_28_672357894#5_1448460934","relevance":3,"reason":"The document is dedicated to developing humility and directly explains that cultivating humility and letting go of shortcomings can make a person happier, more fulfilled, and more spiritually connected, with practices such as gratitude and kindness.","learned":"Humility can lead to a better life by helping people let go of past shortcomings, become happier and more fulfilled, deepen spiritual connection, practice gratitude, avoid unhealthy comparison, and act kindly."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q3086","reason":"The direct humility-to-happiness query produced a strong dedicated result, so continue to look for more documents with similarly explicit explanations."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q3086"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_28_672357894#4_1448458718","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q3086","rank":2,"snippet":"that important Fourth Step of AA, you had to put your ego aside and perform a searching and fearless moral inventory to uncover the roots of your alcohol addiction. In Step Five you had to tell another person the exact nature of your wrongs and in Step 6 you had to revisit your inventory to uncover the character flaws that kept you stuck in your addiction. These previous steps allowed you to start cultivating and practicing humility and the act of letting go those shortcomings that marked your past life will help you become <cover>happier, more fulfilled and more spiritually connected. 5 Ways to Practice Humility </cover>in Your Recovery If you are about to work or are currently working the Seventh Step of AA, the following five ways can help humility flourish in your recovery and your life: Practice Gratitude It is important to look at what positive attributes you have and how you can share them with others. Practicing gratitude in your recovery on a daily basis will allow you to truly be grounded within yourself without bragging or have an inflated sense of worth. Be Yourself Don’t fall into the trap with comparing yourself to other people."}}
