{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_40_1103074658#4_2319986357","relevance":3,"reason":"This is another segment of the Forbes article dedicated to reasons humility helps people get ahead; it directly says humility brings new perspectives, stronger relationships, happier customers, personal and professional growth, trust, confidence, loyalty, and magnifies other strengths.","learned":"Humility improves life by grounding people, opening them to resources and possibilities, strengthening trust and relationships, and supporting personal and professional growth."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"intellectual humility\" (+ wellbeing \"well-being\" flourishing happiness) (+ relationships growth))","reason":"Search a distinct evidence area: intellectual humility research, which may directly link humility with well-being, growth, relationships, and flourishing."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"intellectual humility\" (+ wellbeing \"well-being\" flourishing happiness) (+ relationships growth))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_54_41702696#10_116081575","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q3087","rank":1,"snippet":"\" , \"segment\": \"But even these other-reporting measures have limitations since observers’ perceptions may themselves be biased. They may, for instance, attribute higher levels to people who agree with their beliefs and values than to those who do not. Following insights from research on general humility, intellectual humility might best be observed by others in certain kinds of situations: during interpersonal conflict, while receiving praise, in hierarchical <cover>relationships, or in interactions across different cultures or among those who embrace different norms. Finally, related fields such as cognitive neuroscience may soon yield alternative ways of measurement. Recent work using EEGs to measure subjects’ brain activity when they make errors points to potentially less subjective ways of measuring this trait. INTELLECTUAL HUMILITY AND WELL-BEING</cover>Researchers tend to presume that intellectual humility is better for people than contrasting traits such as intellectual arrogance and closed-mindedness. Some claim in particular that intellectual humility improves well-being, enhances tolerance for other perspectives, and promotes inquiry and learning. Such claims, if true, would show why encouraging people to grow in intellectual humility is worth the effort. But at present there are many more unsettled questions than well-supported answers."}}
{"request":{"judgments":"15/50"}}
{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_54_41702696#10_116081575","relevance":2,"reason":"The document appears to be dedicated to intellectual humility and has a section on well-being, with claims that intellectual humility may improve well-being, tolerance, inquiry, and learning; however, the snippet is cautious and says the evidence is unsettled, so it is not yet clear enough for grade 3 from the snippet alone.","learned":"Intellectual humility is hypothesized to improve the good life through well-being, tolerance for other perspectives, inquiry, and learning, though this source may emphasize unsettled evidence."},"action":{"op":"document","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_54_41702696#10_116081575","reason":"The snippet is promising but cautious; the full document may contain a dedicated section with direct evidence on intellectual humility and well-being."}}
{"request":{"op":"document","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_54_41702696#10_116081575"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_54_41702696#10_116081575","document":"Intellectual Humility - Recent Research - John Templeton Foundation ... Intellectual Humility Character Virtue Development Intellectual Humility DEFINITIONS MEASURING INTELLECTUAL HUMILITY INTELLECTUAL HUMILITY AND WELL-BEING ENHANCING TOLERANCE A TOOL FOR LEARNING STRATEGIES FOR INCREASING INTELLECTUAL HUMILITY DIRECTIONS FOR FUTURE INQUIRY STILL CURIOUS?  ... But even these other-reporting measures have limitations since observers’ perceptions may themselves be biased. They may, for instance, attribute higher levels to people who agree with their beliefs and values than to those who do not. Following insights from research on general humility, intellectual humility might best be observed by others in certain kinds of situations: during interpersonal conflict, while receiving praise, in hierarchical relationships, or in interactions across different cultures or among those who embrace different norms. Finally, related fields such as cognitive neuroscience may soon yield alternative ways of measurement. Recent work using EEGs to measure subjects’ brain activity when they make errors points to potentially less subjective ways of measuring this trait. INTELLECTUAL HUMILITY AND WELL-BEING Researchers tend to presume that intellectual humility is better for people than contrasting traits such as intellectual arrogance and closed-mindedness. Some claim in particular that intellectual humility improves well-being, enhances tolerance for other perspectives, and promotes inquiry and learning. Such claims, if true, would show why encouraging people to grow in intellectual humility is worth the effort. But at present there are many more unsettled questions than well-supported answers.","ok":true,"op":"document"}}
