{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_20_1541559733#3_3367591944","relevance":3,"reason":"The article is dedicated to why humility is good and directly explains that humility/quiet ego reduces aggression, manipulation, dishonesty, and destructiveness while increasing responsibility for mistakes, openness to others' ideas, realistic self-perspective, and benefits for individuals and relationships.","learned":"Humility leads to a better life by quieting the ego: it reduces harmful self-protective behaviors and supports responsibility, teachability, better relationships, and healthier leadership."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ humility (+ \"quiet ego\" ego) (+ well-being relationships))","reason":"The Greater Good result points to the 'quiet ego' construct as a research-backed mechanism; searching it may uncover more evidence on humility, well-being, and relationships without relying on duplicate segments."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ humility (+ \"quiet ego\" ego) (+ well-being relationships))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_23_503115412#8_1103052973","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q3098","rank":1,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_23_503115412#8_1103052973\" , \"end_char\": 4631.000000 , \"headings\": \"4 Ways to Overcome the Danger of False Humility 4 Ways to Overcome the Danger of False Humility Like this: \" , \"segment\": \"Instead of focusing on yourself, focus on serving others. As the old saying goes, humility is not thinking less of yourself, it’s thinking about yourself less. Like this: Like Loading... Like 11 bloggers like this. 4 Comments Posted on October 6, 2019 by Randy Conley Category: Authenticity, Credibility, Ego, Humility, Integrity, Narcissism, Power, Relationships Tags: Authenticity, <cover>Ego, Humble, Humility, Relationships ← </cover>25 Simple Ways to Build Trust at Work The 1 Thing That Makes Feedback Work and 4 Ways to Get It →\" , \"start_char\": 4111.000000 , \"title\": \"4 Ways to Overcome the Danger of False Humility | Leading with Trust\" , \"url\": \"https://leadingwithtrust.com/2019/10/06/4-ways-to-overcome-the-danger-of-false-humility/\" }"}}
